# 2026-09-13 — full live KB; development probes, never persisted training.
# A definition is not evidence for a stranded relation. Partitive objects keep
# their domain. The invented storage examples below test runtime mechanics,
# not knowledge of the world or connecting dots.

[test definition fits the requested relation]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset
!timeout 30
> what is calcium carbonate?
<~ CaCO3
> what is calcium carbonate for?
<! CaCO3
!query definition_unfilled_relation(current_turn)
> what is calcium carbonate from?
<! CaCO3
> what is a compass used for?
<~ finding north
> what is calcium carbonate?
<~ CaCO3

[test a spoken preposition changes definition eligibility]
!reset
!timeout 30
> what is calcium carbonate aboard?
<~ CaCO3
> aboard is a preposition
<~ Learned
> what is calcium carbonate aboard?
<! CaCO3
!query definition_unfilled_relation(current_turn)
> forget that aboard is a preposition
<~ Forgotten
> what is calcium carbonate aboard?
<~ CaCO3
> aboard is a preposition
<~ Learned
> what is calcium carbonate aboard?
<! CaCO3

[test partitive transfer and complement boundary]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Shallow coral reefs form some of Earth's most diverse ecosystems.
<~ diverse ecosystems
> what do shallow coral reefs form?
<~ diverse ecosystems
> Organisms occupy many of the coastal habitats.
<~ many of the coastal habitats
> what do organisms occupy?
<~ Many of the coastal habitats
> Forests occupy half of the global land area.
<~ half of the global land area
> what do forests occupy?
<~ Half of the global land area
> Workers occupy all of the sheltered spaces.
<~ all of the sheltered spaces
> what do workers occupy?
<~ All of the sheltered spaces
> Coral belongs to the class Anthozoa in the animal phylum Cnidaria.
<~ class anthozoa
> what does coral belong to?
< Class anthozoa.

[test new partitive head grows and retracts without rebuilding]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Boxes occupy a handful of the storage spaces.
<! handful of the storage spaces
!assert measure_noun(handful)
> Crates occupy a handful of the storage spaces.
<~ handful of the storage spaces
> what do crates occupy?
<~ Handful of the storage spaces
!forget measure_noun(handful)
> Baskets occupy a handful of the storage spaces.
<! handful of the storage spaces
!assert measure_noun(handful)
> Trunks occupy a handful of the storage spaces.
<~ handful of the storage spaces

[test removing the quantifier bridge removes the complete reading]
!reset
!timeout 30
!forget partitive_head_class(non_universal_quantifier)
> Collectors occupy several of the coastal habitats.
<! several of the coastal habitats
!assert partitive_head_class(non_universal_quantifier)
> Visitors occupy several of the coastal habitats.
<~ several of the coastal habitats
